---
import {products,brandFor} from '../data/catalog';
const {a,b}=Astro.props;const keys=[...new Set([...Object.keys(a.specs),...Object.keys(b.specs)])];
---
<div class="answer"><span class="kicker">The quick answer</span><p>Choose the {a.model} {a.use==='weekend'?'for a relaxed, upright ride':a.use==='commute'?'for a commuter-focused setup with suspension':'for a simpler city setup'}. The {b.model} is the alternative {b.use==='city'?'for a pared-back urban routine':'when its riding position and equipment better match your route'}. Start with fit and storage, then compare the specifications below.</p></div><div class="compare-scroll"><table class="compare-table"><caption class="hidden">Bike specifications and rider fit comparison</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The shortlist</th>{[a,b].map(p=><th scope="col"><a class="product-image" href={`/reviews/${p.slug}`}><img src={p.image} width="600" height="400" alt={p.name}/></a><h2>{p.name}</h2><p>{p.label}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/reviews/${p.slug}`}>Full review →</a></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{keys.map(k=><tr><th scope="row">{k}</th>{[a,b].map(p=><td>{p.specs[k]||'Not listed here'}</td>)}</tr>)}<tr><th scope="row">Consider</th>{[a,b].map(p=><td>{p.tradeoffs[0]}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Next step</th>{[a,b].map(p=><td><a class="text-link" href={p.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener">See {brandFor(p).name} ↗</a></td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div><p class="disclosure">Manufacturer specifications checked October 19, 2026. Range figures are manufacturer claims, not comparable independent range tests. Check the selected configuration before ordering.</p>
